    "notes": "Five parts: Descant, Soprano, Alto, Tenor, Bass. S+A share the treble staff and T+B the bass staff (closed score - split by stem direction). The Descant staff (75 % size) is hidden in the verse 1-3 systems (truth: invisible measure rests) and appears for verse 4; its first three measures are CUE-SIZE notes of the melody (encoded <cue/>, not sung): a correct conversion marks them as cue notes or omits them (rests) - they must not become sounding Descant notes and carry no lyrics. The hymn is written out twice (verses 1-3, then verse 4 + descant: the last bar of pass 1 and the pickup of pass 2 are both 2-beat measures). The final \"Amen\" (2 measures) is a separate smaller system (78 % staff size) continuing the S/A/T/B parts; the Descant has invisible rests there. Lyrics: Soprano lines 1-3 in pass 1, line 4 (Doxology) in pass 2, line 1 \"A-men\"; Descant line 1 from its 4th measure."
  },
